committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790600417 +0900

Cache BM25 indexes per source snapshot; add E3 driver

The first E1 launch was CPU-bound: every writer call rebuilt a BM25 index
over all in-scope objects. Indexes are now built once per (log, time,
declared sources, delta) and shared by all cells and slots, with a token
cache per object revision; SourceLog carries a unique id for cache keys.
Adds the E3 driver (static ContractValid at 1/3/12 months for zero, RAG,
HoldMem (1,1) and oracle; five-part cost model with counted daily-batch
invalidations x measured unit cost) and an option to build HoldMem with
the full D=1 write path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
